# Advent of Code 2025, day 10 part 2 (Factory), with the puzzle's example as input (answer 33)
#
# THE PUZZLE
# Each line of the input is a machine with a row of counters, all 0 at the start, the joltage each
# counter must reach, and a number of buttons, each wired to some of the counters. Pushing a button
# adds 1 to each of its counters. The answer is the fewest pushes that bring every counter of a
# machine exactly to its joltage, added up over all machines. (The light patterns are not used.)
#
# THE IDEA
# Look at which counters must end odd. Whatever the pushes are, the buttons pushed an odd number of
# times decide that. So pick a set S of buttons, pushed once each, that makes exactly the right
# counters odd. What is then left to reach is even on every counter, and it must be made by pushing
# buttons an even number of times: that is the same puzzle with all joltages halved, counted twice.
#     FEWEST(B) = the smallest, over all such sets S, of (buttons in S) + 2 * FEWEST((B - what S adds) / 2)
#     FEWEST(all 0) = 0
# A set that would push a counter past its joltage is left out. The joltages halve each time, so
# this goes at most as deep as the largest joltage has bits.
# The example's first machine, joltages 3,5,4,7 (odd: counters 0, 1, 3): one set that makes these odd is
# (3), (0,1): it leaves 2,4,4,6, halved 1,2,2,3, and FEWEST(1,2,2,3) = 4, so 2 + 2 * 4 = 10.
#   - Which sets S? "Odd or even" is part 1's lights: a button's counters are the bits of a word, and a
#     set's effect is the xor of its buttons. While reading the buttons the program keeps a BASIS:
#     button words reduced so that each has a lowest bit of its own, each with the set of buttons it
#     was made from. A button word that reduces to nothing gives a set of buttons that changes no
#     counter's oddness: a NULL set. Reducing the wanted pattern by the BASIS gives one set that makes
#     it; all the others are that set xor some of the NULL sets (2, 4, 8 or 16 sets in all, usually).
#   - The same joltages come up again and again down different ways, so every result is kept in a
#     table (MEMO), found again by a number worked out from the joltages (a hash).
#
# THE WHOLE PROGRAM IN PSEUDO CODE
#     TOTAL = 0
#     for each machine:
#         step over the lights
#         for each button: remember where its counters are listed; put its word through the BASIS
#         B = the joltages
#         FEWEST; TOTAL = TOTAL + RET
#     write TOTAL as five decimal digits
#     stop
#
#     FEWEST:                                               # works on B, leaves the answer in RET
#         if B is all 0: RET = 0; return
#         if B is in MEMO: RET = its value; return
#         V = the word of the odd counters of B; C = 0; REDUCE          # C becomes one set that makes them odd
#         BEST = 0xFFFF                                     # "cannot be done"
#         if V == 0:                                        # the pattern can be made
#             S = C
#             for G = 0; G != GEND; G = G + 1:              # GEND = 2 to the power (number of NULL sets)
#                 if G != 0: S = S xor NULL[the place of the lowest 1 bit of G]     # the next set, every one once
#                 W = B; for every button of S, every counter of the button: W[counter] -= 1 (stop if it is 0)
#                 if that worked: keep B, S, G, BEST; B = W / 2; FEWEST; get them back
#                                 if RET != 0xFFFF and (buttons in S) + 2 * RET < BEST: BEST = that
#         put B with BEST into MEMO; RET = BEST
#
# THE RESULT, when the CPU stops on the Breakpoint at END
#   0x0100         the total as one 16-bit word
#   0x0110-0x0114  the total as five decimal digits, one per word, most significant first
#
# THE INPUT (rule 1 of RULES.md), at 0x2000, the same words as in part 1
# Machine after machine, as in the puzzle's text:
#     one word per light: 0 for off (.), 1 for on (#); then 0xFFFF
#     for each button: the numbers of its counters, then 0xFFFE; after the last button 0xFFFF
#     the joltages, one word each; then 0xFFFF
# After the last machine comes one more 0xFFFF.
# Built-in limits: at most 10 counters and 16 buttons a machine; a button names a counter once;
# joltages below 32,768; every machine can be set; at most about 1,500 different joltage rows come up
# for one machine (MEMO has room for 2,048); the total stays below 65,536.
#
# ONE WORD IS ENOUGH
# Every value here fits in 16 bits, so each variable is one memory word. The idioms used everywhere
# (v is a variable's address, below 0x1000):
#     getA v                   A = the word at v   (lia v; load rgA rgA: lia puts the address in A, load replaces it)
#     getB v                   B = the word at v
#     putA v                   the word at v = A   (this uses up B)
#     getAat p / putAat p      the same for the word the pointer p points at
#     getAoff p k              A = the word at the address (p + k)
#     copy v w                 w = v
#     if_eq L / if_neq L       compares A with B as they are now
#     sub; if_carry L          after A - B: taken when A >= B
# Halving: shf | 15 moves a word 15 places up in A; the upper half of A is then the word / 2.
# FEWEST calls itself. What it must keep goes on the CPU's stack with psh and comes back with pop.
# What each instruction does exactly is in findings/cpu-instructions.md.
#
# MEMORY MAP
#   0x0100-0x015F  variables            0x0200-0x0209  B: the joltages at hand     0x0210-0x0219  W
#   0x0220-0x0229  BASISV: the reduced button words, by their lowest bit           0x0230-0x0239  BASISC: their sets
#   0x0240-0x024F  NULL: the sets that change no oddness      0x0250-0x025F  BLIST: where each button's counters are
#   0x1000-        the program          0x1800-  the subroutines
#   0x1E00-        POWERS: 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1, 0         0x1E10-  BITS: 1, 2, 4, ..., 32768
#   0x2000-        the input (3 machines end at 0x205E)
#   0x8000-0xDFFF  MEMO: 2,048 places of 12 words: the machine's number, the value, the ten joltages
#   0xE000-        the CPU's stack
#   0xFF00         where the CPU starts

# ---- The CPU's instructions as symbols (day 1's table without its _32 names, which the CPU ignores) ----
symbol nop 0b0000_0000_0000_0000            # the word 0: stops the CPU (the same word as non)
symbol ld  0b0010_0000_0000_0000            # load a register from memory (used through the load macro)
symbol lia 0b0011_0000_0000_0000            # lia n: A = n (0 to 4095), upper half 0
symbol lib 0b0100_0000_0000_0000            # lib n: B = n (0 to 4095), upper half 0
symbol sto 0b0101_0000_0000_0000            # store a register to memory (used through the store macro)

macro  load  { ld  | a? | (b? >> 6) }       # load X Y: X = the word at the address in Y
macro  store { sto | a? | (b? >> 6) }       # store X Y: the word at the address in Y = X

symbol sum    0b0110_0100_0000_0000         # A = A + B (32 bits), sets zero, carry, nega
symbol sub    0b0110_0010_0000_0000         # A = A - B (32 bits), sets zero, carry, nega
symbol shf    0b0110_0001_0000_0000         # shf | k: A = A shifted left by k (0 to 15)
symbol and    0b0110_0000_1000_0000         # A = A and B
symbol or     0b0110_0000_0100_0000         # A = A or B
symbol xor    0b0110_0000_0010_0000         # A = A xor B
symbol neg    0b0110_0000_0001_0000         # A = every bit of A flipped

symbol psh 0b1010_0000_0000_0000            # psh X: push the 16 bits of X
symbol pop 0b1011_0000_0000_0000            # pop X: pop 16 bits into X

symbol jmp  0b1100_0000_0000_0000           # jmp; L: go to L.  jmp c; L: go to L when c holds
symbol call 0b1110_0000_0000_0000           # call; L: run the subroutine at L
symbol ret  0b1111_0000_0000_0000           # return from a subroutine

# The registers, as load, store, psh and pop name them
symbol rgAH 0b1000_0000_0000                # the upper 16 bits of A
symbol rgA  0b0100_0000_0000                # the lower 16 bits of A
symbol rgBH 0b0010_0000_0000                # the upper 16 bits of B
symbol rgB  0b0001_0000_0000                # the lower 16 bits of B
symbol rgSP 0b0000_1000_0000                # the program counter (leave alone)
symbol rgSB 0b0000_0100_0000                # the stack pointer (leave alone)
symbol non  0                               # stops the CPU (Breakpoint): the end of the program

# The conditions of jmp
symbol zero  0b1000_0000_0000               # the last sum or sub gave 0
symbol carry 0b0100_0000_0000               # the last sum carried, or the last sub did not borrow (A >= B)
symbol nega  0b0010_0000_0000               # the last sub went below 0 (A < B)
symbol eq    0b0001_0000_0000               # A == B right now
symbol neq   0b0000_1000_0000               # A != B right now

# ---- Macros for the common operations (explained in the README). A macro cannot use another macro, so
#      load and store are spelled out here. v: a variable, p: a variable holding an address, L: a label ----
macro getA     { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6) }                                              # A = v
macro getB     { lib a?; ld | rgB | (rgB >> 6) }                                              # B = v
macro putA     { lib a?; sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }                                             # v = A (uses B)
macro getAat   { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6) }                       # A = the word p points at
macro putAat   { lib a?; ld | rgB | (rgB >> 6); sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }                      # the word p points at = A (uses B)
macro inc      { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); lib 1; sum; lib a?; sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }  # v = v + 1 (uses A and B)
macro goto     { jmp; a? }                                                                    # go to L
macro if_eq    { jmp eq; a? }                                                                 # go to L when A == B
macro do       { call; a? }                                                                   # call the subroutine L
macro if_carry { jmp carry; a? }                                                              # go to L after a sub when A >= B
macro getAoff  { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); lib b?; sum; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6) }                # A = the word at (p + k) (uses B)
macro copy     { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); lib b?; sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }                      # w = v (uses A and B)
macro if_neq   { jmp neq; a? }                                                                # go to L when A != B

# ---- Variables (all below 0x1000, so lia/lib can address them) ----
# The result
pointer TOTAL 0x0100 0
# IN: the address of the next word of the input
pointer IN 0x0120 0x2000
# For reading a button: MASK its word, BBIT the word of its place among the buttons (1, 2, 4, ...), BL where its list address goes
pointer MASK 0x0121 0
pointer BBIT 0x0122 0
pointer BL 0x0123 0
# BL_END: the address after the last word of BLIST. NULL_END: the same for NULL. GEND: 2 to the power (number of NULL sets)
pointer BL_END 0x0124 0
pointer NULL_END 0x0125 0
pointer GEND 0x0126 0
# For REDUCE: V the word being reduced, C the set that goes with it, PV and PC places in BASISV and BASISC, BITV the bit looked at
pointer V 0x0127 0
pointer C 0x0128 0
pointer PV 0x0129 0
pointer PC 0x012A 0
pointer BITV 0x012B 0
# BP: where the next joltage goes in B. STAMP: the number of the machine. RET: what FEWEST returns
pointer BP 0x012C 0
pointer STAMP 0x012D 0
pointer RET 0x012E 0
# For FEWEST: S the set of buttons being tried, G its number, BEST the fewest pushes so far, CNT the buttons in S, CAND = CNT + 2 * RET
pointer S 0x012F 0
pointer G 0x0130 0
pointer BEST 0x0131 0
pointer CNT 0x0132 0
pointer CAND 0x0133 0
# NP, TZB: for finding the lowest 1 bit of G
pointer NP 0x0134 0
pointer TZB 0x0135 0
# For TRY_S: OK is 1 when S pushes no counter too far, SBIT the word of the button looked at, LP a place in its list, ADR an address
pointer OK 0x0136 0
pointer SBIT 0x0137 0
pointer LP 0x0138 0
pointer ADR 0x0139 0
# For LOOKUP: H the hash, SLOT the place in MEMO, KP a place in its key, HIT 1 when B is there, VALUE its value
pointer H 0x013A 0
pointer SLOT 0x013B 0
pointer KP 0x013C 0
pointer HIT 0x013D 0
pointer VALUE 0x013E 0
# For the decimal digits: what is left of the total, the current power of ten, how often it fitted
pointer REST 0x013F 0
pointer POWER 0x0140 0
pointer DIGIT_VALUE 0x0141 0
# Pointers: DIGIT the next digit to write, POW the next power of ten
pointer DIGIT 0x0142 0x0110
pointer POW 0x0143 0x1E00
# Constants that do not fit an instruction's place for a number
pointer B_BASE 0x0144 0x0200
pointer W_BASE 0x0145 0x0210
pointer BASISV 0x0146 0x0220
pointer BASISC 0x0147 0x0230
pointer NULLS 0x0148 0x0240
pointer BLIST 0x0149 0x0250
pointer BITS 0x014A 0x1E10
pointer MEMO 0x014B 0x8000
pointer HMASK 0x014C 0x07FF
pointer END_MARK 0x014D 0xFFFF
pointer BUTTON_MARK 0x014E 0xFFFE
pointer INF 0x014F 0xFFFF
# B: the joltages still to reach. W: B after the pushes of S, halved
pointer B0 0x0200 0
pointer B1 0x0201 0
pointer B2 0x0202 0
pointer B3 0x0203 0
pointer B4 0x0204 0
pointer B5 0x0205 0
pointer B6 0x0206 0
pointer B7 0x0207 0
pointer B8 0x0208 0
pointer B9 0x0209 0
pointer W0 0x0210 0
pointer W1 0x0211 0
pointer W2 0x0212 0
pointer W3 0x0213 0
pointer W4 0x0214 0
pointer W5 0x0215 0
pointer W6 0x0216 0
pointer W7 0x0217 0
pointer W8 0x0218 0
pointer W9 0x0219 0
# BV: the words of BASISV, by name, for clearing them
pointer BV0 0x0220 0
pointer BV1 0x0221 0
pointer BV2 0x0222 0
pointer BV3 0x0223 0
pointer BV4 0x0224 0
pointer BV5 0x0225 0
pointer BV6 0x0226 0
pointer BV7 0x0227 0
pointer BV8 0x0228 0
pointer BV9 0x0229 0

# ---- The CPU starts at 0xFF00 ----
origin 0xFF00
goto MAIN

origin 0x1000
@ MAIN
# ==== read a machine: step over its lights ====
#     if memory[IN] == 0xFFFF: goto ALL_DONE                # no machine is left
#     while memory[IN] != 0xFFFF: IN = IN + 1
#     IN = IN + 1
@ NEXT_MACHINE
	getAat IN; getB END_MARK                                     # A = memory[IN], B = 0xFFFF
	if_eq ALL_DONE                                               # the end of the input
@ LIGHT
	inc IN                                                       # IN = IN + 1
	load rgA rgA; getB END_MARK                                  # A = memory[IN] (A still held IN), B = 0xFFFF
	if_neq LIGHT
	inc IN                                                       # IN = IN + 1: past the 0xFFFF

# ==== its buttons ====
#     BASISV = all 0; NULL = empty; GEND = 1; BBIT = 1; BL = BLIST
#     while memory[IN] != 0xFFFF:
#         memory[BL] = IN; BL = BL + 1                      # where this button's counters are listed
#         MASK = 0
#         while memory[IN] != 0xFFFE: MASK = MASK + BITS[memory[IN]]; IN = IN + 1
#         IN = IN + 1
#         V = MASK; C = BBIT; REDUCE
#         if V != 0: memory[PV] = V; memory[PC] = C         # a new word of the BASIS, at its lowest bit
#         else: memory[NULL_END] = C; NULL_END = NULL_END + 1; GEND = GEND * 2      # a NULL set
#         BBIT = BBIT * 2
#     BL_END = BL; IN = IN + 1
	lia 0; putA BV0; putA BV1; putA BV2; putA BV3; putA BV4      # BASISV = all 0; words 0 to 4
	putA BV5; putA BV6; putA BV7; putA BV8; putA BV9             # words 5 to 9 (A still holds 0)
	copy NULLS NULL_END                                          # NULL is empty
	lia 1; putA GEND; putA BBIT                                  # GEND = 1; BBIT = 1
	copy BLIST BL                                                # BL = the first word of BLIST
@ BUTTON
	getAat IN; getB END_MARK                                     # A = memory[IN], B = 0xFFFF
	if_eq BUTTONS_DONE                                           # the end of the buttons
	getA IN; putAat BL                                           # memory[BL] = IN
	inc BL                                                       # BL = BL + 1
	lia 0; putA MASK                                             # MASK = 0
@ BUTTON_COUNTER
	getAat IN; getB BUTTON_MARK                                  # A = memory[IN], B = 0xFFFE
	if_eq BUTTON_END                                             # the end of this button
	getB BITS; sum; load rgA rgA                                 # A = BITS[the number of the counter]
	getB MASK; sum; putA MASK                                    # MASK = MASK + that
	inc IN                                                       # IN = IN + 1
	goto BUTTON_COUNTER
@ BUTTON_END
	inc IN                                                       # IN = IN + 1: past the 0xFFFE
	copy MASK V; copy BBIT C                                     # V = MASK; C = this button alone
	do REDUCE
	getA V; lib 0                                                # A = V, B = 0
	if_eq BUTTON_NULL                                            # nothing is left of it
	putAat PV                                                    # memory[PV] = V (A still holds V)
	getA C; putAat PC                                            # memory[PC] = C
	goto BUTTON_NEXT
@ BUTTON_NULL
	getA C; putAat NULL_END                                      # memory[NULL_END] = C
	inc NULL_END                                                 # NULL_END = NULL_END + 1
	getA GEND; shf | 1; putA GEND                                # GEND = GEND * 2
@ BUTTON_NEXT
	getA BBIT; shf | 1; putA BBIT                                # BBIT = BBIT * 2
	goto BUTTON
@ BUTTONS_DONE
	copy BL BL_END                                               # BL_END = the address after the last word of BLIST
	inc IN                                                       # IN = IN + 1: past the 0xFFFF

# ==== its joltages, and the fewest pushes ====
#     B = all 0
#     for BP = B_BASE; memory[IN] != 0xFFFF; BP = BP + 1, IN = IN + 1: memory[BP] = memory[IN]
#     IN = IN + 1
#     STAMP = STAMP + 1                                     # MEMO's places of other machines no longer count
#     FEWEST; TOTAL = TOTAL + RET
	lia 0; putA B0; putA B1; putA B2; putA B3; putA B4           # B = all 0; words 0 to 4
	putA B5; putA B6; putA B7; putA B8; putA B9                  # words 5 to 9 (A still holds 0)
	copy B_BASE BP                                               # BP = the first word of B
@ JOLTAGE
	getAat IN; getB END_MARK                                     # A = memory[IN], B = 0xFFFF
	if_eq JOLTAGES_DONE
	putAat BP                                                    # memory[BP] = the joltage (A still holds it)
	inc BP                                                       # BP = BP + 1
	inc IN                                                       # IN = IN + 1
	goto JOLTAGE
@ JOLTAGES_DONE
	inc IN                                                       # IN = IN + 1: past the 0xFFFF
	inc STAMP                                                    # STAMP = STAMP + 1
	do FEWEST                                                    # RET = the fewest pushes for this machine
	getA TOTAL; getB RET; sum; putA TOTAL                        # TOTAL = TOTAL + RET
	goto NEXT_MACHINE

# ==== write TOTAL as five decimal digits ====
# A digit is how often a power of ten fits into what is left. Without division that is counting:
#     REST = TOTAL
#     for POWER in 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1:
#         DIGIT_VALUE = 0
#         while REST >= POWER: REST = REST - POWER; DIGIT_VALUE = DIGIT_VALUE + 1
#         memory[DIGIT] = DIGIT_VALUE; DIGIT = DIGIT + 1
# After sub, the carry flag is set when A >= B (no borrow).
@ ALL_DONE
	getA TOTAL; putA REST                                        # REST = TOTAL
@ NEXT_POWER
	getAat POW                                                   # A = memory[POW], the next power of ten
	putA POWER                                                   # POWER = A
	lib 0                                                        # B = 0
	if_eq END                                                    # a power of 0 ends the table
	inc POW                                                      # POW = POW + 1
	lia 0; putA DIGIT_VALUE                                      # DIGIT_VALUE = 0
@ FITS_AGAIN
	getA REST; getB POWER                                        # A = REST, B = POWER
	sub                                                          # A = REST - POWER
	if_carry FITS                                                # REST >= POWER: it fits once more
	getA DIGIT_VALUE; putAat DIGIT                                       # memory[DIGIT] = DIGIT_VALUE   (B holds the address in DIGIT)
	inc DIGIT                                                    # DIGIT = DIGIT + 1
	goto NEXT_POWER
@ FITS
	putA REST                                                    # REST = REST - POWER   (A still holds the difference)
	inc DIGIT_VALUE                                                          # DIGIT_VALUE = DIGIT_VALUE + 1
	goto FITS_AGAIN

# The word 0 stops the CPU on its Breakpoint.
@ END
	non
# ---- Subroutines ----
origin 0x1800
# REDUCE: xor words of the BASIS into V until nothing is left of it or no word fits; C gets the same sets.
# The word at place i of BASISV, if there is one, has bit i as its lowest bit.
#     PV = BASISV; PC = BASISC; BITV = 1
#     while V != 0:
#         if (V and BITV) != 0:
#             if memory[PV] == 0: return                    # no word with this lowest bit: V stays, PV and PC say where it would go
#             V = V xor memory[PV]; C = C xor memory[PC]
#         PV = PV + 1; PC = PC + 1; BITV = BITV * 2
@ REDUCE
	copy BASISV PV; copy BASISC PC                               # PV, PC = the first words of the BASIS
	lia 1; putA BITV                                             # BITV = 1
@ REDUCE_BIT
	getA V; lib 0                                                # A = V, B = 0
	if_eq REDUCE_DONE                                            # nothing is left of V
	getB BITV; and; lib 0                                        # A = V and BITV, B = 0
	if_eq REDUCE_NEXT                                            # V does not have this bit
	getAat PV; lib 0                                             # A = the word of the BASIS with this lowest bit, B = 0
	if_eq REDUCE_DONE                                            # there is none
	getB V; xor; putA V                                          # V = V xor that word
	getAat PC; getB C; xor; putA C                               # C = C xor its set
@ REDUCE_NEXT
	inc PV                                                       # PV = PV + 1
	inc PC                                                       # PC = PC + 1
	getA BITV; shf | 1; putA BITV                                # BITV = BITV * 2
	goto REDUCE_BIT
@ REDUCE_DONE
	ret

# FEWEST: RET = the fewest pushes that add up to B, or 0xFFFF when it cannot be done. (Pseudo code: at the top.)
@ FEWEST
	getA B0; getB B1; sum; getB B2; sum; getB B3; sum; getB B4; sum # A = B0 + B1 + B2 + B3 + B4
	getB B5; sum; getB B6; sum; getB B7; sum; getB B8; sum; getB B9; sum # A = the sum of all of B
	lib 0                                                        # B = 0
	if_neq FEWEST_SOME
	lia 0; putA RET                                              # B is all 0: RET = 0
	ret
@ FEWEST_SOME
	do LOOKUP                                                    # is B in MEMO?
	getA HIT; lib 0                                              # A = HIT, B = 0
	if_eq FEWEST_NEW
	copy VALUE RET                                               # RET = the value kept there
	ret
@ FEWEST_NEW
	lia 0; putA V; putA C                                        # V = 0; C = 0
	getA B0; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B0 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_0
	getA V; lib 1; sum; putA V                                   # counter 0 is odd: V = V + 1
@ EVEN_0
	getA B1; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B1 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_1
	getA V; lib 2; sum; putA V                                   # counter 1 is odd: V = V + 2
@ EVEN_1
	getA B2; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B2 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_2
	getA V; lib 4; sum; putA V                                   # counter 2 is odd: V = V + 4
@ EVEN_2
	getA B3; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B3 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_3
	getA V; lib 8; sum; putA V                                   # counter 3 is odd: V = V + 8
@ EVEN_3
	getA B4; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B4 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_4
	getA V; lib 16; sum; putA V                                  # counter 4 is odd: V = V + 16
@ EVEN_4
	getA B5; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B5 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_5
	getA V; lib 32; sum; putA V                                  # counter 5 is odd: V = V + 32
@ EVEN_5
	getA B6; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B6 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_6
	getA V; lib 64; sum; putA V                                  # counter 6 is odd: V = V + 64
@ EVEN_6
	getA B7; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B7 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_7
	getA V; lib 128; sum; putA V                                 # counter 7 is odd: V = V + 128
@ EVEN_7
	getA B8; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B8 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_8
	getA V; lib 256; sum; putA V                                 # counter 8 is odd: V = V + 256
@ EVEN_8
	getA B9; lib 1; and; lib 0                                   # A = B9 and 1, B = 0
	if_eq EVEN_9
	getA V; lib 512; sum; putA V                                 # counter 9 is odd: V = V + 512
@ EVEN_9
	do REDUCE                                                    # C = one set of buttons that makes these counters odd
	copy INF BEST                                                # BEST = 0xFFFF
	getA V; lib 0                                                # A = V, B = 0
	if_neq FEWEST_KEEP                                           # no set of buttons makes these counters odd
	copy C S                                                     # S = C
	lia 0; putA G                                                # G = 0
@ FEWEST_TRY
	do TRY_S                                                     # W = (B - what S adds) / 2; CNT = the buttons in S; OK = 0 when S pushes too far
	getA OK; lib 0                                               # A = OK, B = 0
	if_eq FEWEST_NEXT
	getA B0; psh rgA; getA B1; psh rgA; getA B2; psh rgA; getA B3; psh rgA; getA B4; psh rgA # keep B on the stack; words 0 to 4
	getA B5; psh rgA; getA B6; psh rgA; getA B7; psh rgA; getA B8; psh rgA; getA B9; psh rgA # keep B on the stack; words 5 to 9
	getA S; psh rgA; getA G; psh rgA; getA BEST; psh rgA; getA CNT; psh rgA # keep S, G, BEST, CNT
	copy W0 B0; copy W1 B1                                       # B = W; words 0 and 1
	copy W2 B2; copy W3 B3                                       # B = W; words 2 and 3
	copy W4 B4; copy W5 B5                                       # B = W; words 4 and 5
	copy W6 B6; copy W7 B7                                       # B = W; words 6 and 7
	copy W8 B8; copy W9 B9                                       # B = W; words 8 and 9
	do FEWEST                                                    # RET = the fewest pushes for the halved joltages
	pop rgA; putA CNT; pop rgA; putA BEST; pop rgA; putA G; pop rgA; putA S # CNT, BEST, G, S come back
	pop rgA; putA B9; pop rgA; putA B8; pop rgA; putA B7; pop rgA; putA B6; pop rgA; putA B5 # B comes back; words 9 down to 5
	pop rgA; putA B4; pop rgA; putA B3; pop rgA; putA B2; pop rgA; putA B1; pop rgA; putA B0 # B comes back; words 4 down to 0
	getA RET; getB INF                                           # A = RET, B = 0xFFFF
	if_eq FEWEST_NEXT                                            # the halved joltages cannot be made
	shf | 1; getB CNT; sum; putA CAND                            # CAND = 2 * RET + CNT
	getB BEST; sub                                               # A = CAND - BEST
	if_carry FEWEST_NEXT                                         # not fewer than BEST
	copy CAND BEST                                               # BEST = CAND
@ FEWEST_NEXT
	inc G                                                        # G = G + 1
	getB GEND                                                    # B = GEND (A still holds G)
	if_eq FEWEST_KEEP                                            # every set has been tried
	copy NULLS NP                                                # NP = the first NULL set
	lia 1; putA TZB                                              # TZB = 1
@ FEWEST_LOWEST
	getA G; getB TZB; and; lib 0                                 # A = G and TZB, B = 0
	if_neq FEWEST_FLIP                                           # this is the lowest 1 bit of G
	inc NP                                                       # NP = NP + 1
	getA TZB; shf | 1; putA TZB                                  # TZB = TZB * 2
	goto FEWEST_LOWEST
@ FEWEST_FLIP
	getAat NP; getB S; xor; putA S                               # S = S xor that NULL set: the next set
	goto FEWEST_TRY
@ FEWEST_KEEP
	do LOOKUP                                                    # SLOT = a free place of MEMO for B
	getA STAMP; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT                            # the place's first word = the machine's number
	getA BEST; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT                             # its second word = BEST
	getA B0; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT; getA B1; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT # then B; words 0 and 1
	getA B2; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT; getA B3; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT # then B; words 2 and 3
	getA B4; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT; getA B5; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT # then B; words 4 and 5
	getA B6; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT; getA B7; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT # then B; words 6 and 7
	getA B8; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT; getA B9; putAat SLOT; inc SLOT # then B; words 8 and 9
	copy BEST RET                                                # RET = BEST
	ret

# TRY_S: W = (B - what the buttons of S add) / 2; CNT = the number of buttons in S; OK = 0 when a counter would go below 0.
#     W = B; CNT = 0; SBIT = 1
#     for BL = BLIST; BL != BL_END; BL = BL + 1:
#         if (S and SBIT) != 0:
#             CNT = CNT + 1
#             for LP = memory[BL]; memory[LP] != 0xFFFE; LP = LP + 1:       # the counters of the button
#                 if W[memory[LP]] == 0: OK = 0; return
#                 W[memory[LP]] = W[memory[LP]] - 1
#         SBIT = SBIT * 2
#     every word of W = itself / 2; OK = 1
@ TRY_S
	copy B0 W0; copy B1 W1                                       # W = B; words 0 and 1
	copy B2 W2; copy B3 W3                                       # W = B; words 2 and 3
	copy B4 W4; copy B5 W5                                       # W = B; words 4 and 5
	copy B6 W6; copy B7 W7                                       # W = B; words 6 and 7
	copy B8 W8; copy B9 W9                                       # W = B; words 8 and 9
	lia 0; putA CNT                                              # CNT = 0
	lia 1; putA SBIT                                             # SBIT = 1
	copy BLIST BL                                                # BL = the first button
@ TRY_BUTTON
	getA BL; getB BL_END                                         # A = BL, B = BL_END
	if_eq TRY_HALVE                                              # every button has been looked at
	getA S; getB SBIT; and; lib 0                                # A = S and SBIT, B = 0
	if_eq TRY_NEXT                                               # this button is not in S
	inc CNT                                                      # CNT = CNT + 1
	getAat BL; putA LP                                           # LP = the button's first counter
@ TRY_COUNTER
	getAat LP; getB BUTTON_MARK                                  # A = memory[LP], B = 0xFFFE
	if_eq TRY_NEXT                                               # the end of the button's counters
	getB W_BASE; sum; putA ADR                                   # ADR = the address of W[that counter]
	load rgA rgA; lib 0                                          # A = W[that counter], B = 0
	if_eq TRY_FAIL                                               # it cannot go lower
	lib 1; sub; putAat ADR                                       # W[that counter] = it - 1
	inc LP                                                       # LP = LP + 1
	goto TRY_COUNTER
@ TRY_NEXT
	inc BL                                                       # BL = BL + 1
	getA SBIT; shf | 1; putA SBIT                                # SBIT = SBIT * 2
	goto TRY_BUTTON
@ TRY_FAIL
	lia 0; putA OK                                               # OK = 0
	ret
@ TRY_HALVE
	getA W0; shf | 15; lib W0; store rgAH rgB; getA W1; shf | 15; lib W1; store rgAH rgB # W = W / 2; words 0 and 1
	getA W2; shf | 15; lib W2; store rgAH rgB; getA W3; shf | 15; lib W3; store rgAH rgB # W = W / 2; words 2 and 3
	getA W4; shf | 15; lib W4; store rgAH rgB; getA W5; shf | 15; lib W5; store rgAH rgB # W = W / 2; words 4 and 5
	getA W6; shf | 15; lib W6; store rgAH rgB; getA W7; shf | 15; lib W7; store rgAH rgB # W = W / 2; words 6 and 7
	getA W8; shf | 15; lib W8; store rgAH rgB; getA W9; shf | 15; lib W9; store rgAH rgB # W = W / 2; words 8 and 9
	lia 1; putA OK                                               # OK = 1
	ret

# LOOKUP: find B in MEMO. A place of MEMO is 12 words: the machine's number, a value, ten joltages.
# HIT = 1 and VALUE = its value when B is there; else HIT = 0 and SLOT = the free place where it belongs.
#     H = B0; for i = 1 to 9: H = H * 9 + Bi                # a number that depends on all of B
#     loop:
#         H = H and 2047; SLOT = MEMO + H * 12
#         if memory[SLOT] != STAMP: HIT = 0; return         # not used for this machine: free
#         if the ten words from SLOT + 2 on are B: HIT = 1; VALUE = memory[SLOT + 1]; return
#         H = H + 1                                         # another row of joltages lives here: try the next place
@ LOOKUP
	copy B0 H                                                    # H = B0
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B1; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B1
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B2; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B2
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B3; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B3
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B4; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B4
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B5; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B5
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B6; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B6
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B7; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B7
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B8; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B8
	getA H; shf | 3; getB H; sum; getB B9; sum; putA H           # H = H * 9 + B9
@ LOOKUP_PLACE
	getA H; getB HMASK; and; putA H                              # H = H and 2047
	shf | 2; putA SLOT                                           # SLOT = H * 4, for now
	getA H; shf | 3; getB SLOT; sum; getB MEMO; sum; putA SLOT   # SLOT = MEMO + H * 8 + H * 4
	load rgA rgA; getB STAMP                                     # A = the place's first word, B = STAMP
	if_neq LOOKUP_FREE                                           # not used for this machine
	getA SLOT; lib 2; sum; putA KP                               # KP = SLOT + 2, the first joltage kept there
	getAat KP; getB B0                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B0
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B1                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B1
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B2                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B2
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B3                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B3
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B4                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B4
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B5                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B5
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B6                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B6
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B7                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B7
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B8                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B8
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	inc KP                                                       # KP = KP + 1
	getAat KP; getB B9                                           # A = the joltage kept, B = B9
	if_neq LOOKUP_OTHER
	getAoff SLOT 1; putA VALUE                                   # VALUE = the value kept there
	lia 1; putA HIT                                              # HIT = 1
	ret
@ LOOKUP_OTHER
	getA H; lib 1; sum; putA H                                   # H = H + 1
	goto LOOKUP_PLACE
@ LOOKUP_FREE
	lia 0; putA HIT                                              # HIT = 0
	ret

# ---- Powers of ten for the decimal digits, then 0 ----
origin 0x1E00
10000; 1000; 100; 10; 1; 0

# ---- The word for each counter: 1, 2, 4, ... ----
origin 0x1E10
1; 2; 4; 8; 16; 32; 64; 128; 256; 512; 1024; 2048; 4096; 8192; 16384; 32768


# ---- The machines: 3, then 0xFFFF ----
origin 0x2000
# [.##.] (3) (1,3) (2) (2,3) (0,2) (0,1) {3,5,4,7}
0; 1; 1; 0; 0xFFFF
3; 0xFFFE; 1; 3; 0xFFFE; 2; 0xFFFE; 2; 3; 0xFFFE; 0; 2; 0xFFFE; 0; 1; 0xFFFE; 0xFFFF
3; 5; 4; 7; 0xFFFF
# [...#.] (0,2,3,4) (2,3) (0,4) (0,1,2) (1,2,3,4) {7,5,12,7,2}
0; 0; 0; 1; 0; 0xFFFF
0; 2; 3; 4; 0xFFFE; 2; 3; 0xFFFE; 0; 4; 0xFFFE; 0; 1; 2; 0xFFFE; 1; 2; 3; 4; 0xFFFE; 0xFFFF
7; 5; 12; 7; 2; 0xFFFF
# [.###.#] (0,1,2,3,4) (0,3,4) (0,1,2,4,5) (1,2) {10,11,11,5,10,5}
0; 1; 1; 1; 0; 1; 0xFFFF
0; 1; 2; 3; 4; 0xFFFE; 0; 3; 4; 0xFFFE; 0; 1; 2; 4; 5; 0xFFFE; 1; 2; 0xFFFE; 0xFFFF
10; 11; 11; 5; 10; 5; 0xFFFF
0xFFFF
